# Keep the image lean: no VCS payload, no venvs, no runtime state (all
# bind-mounted). Everything not needed at runtime is excluded — the context is
# uploaded to the daemon on EVERY build, so big dirs here make
# `docker compose up --build` slow.
#
# .git is excluded EXCEPT the few bytes the Dockerfile reads to derive the build
# stamp itself: `.git/**` drops everything recursively, the !-lines re-include
# HEAD + packed-refs + refs/ (verified on BuildKit 29: objects/, logs/, index,
# hooks/ stay out of the context, and the stamp RUN deletes the leftovers from
# the image). Keep these four lines — without them the stamp degrades to
# "unknown".
.git/**
!.git/HEAD
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs/**
.venv
.venv-linux/
.venv-test/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pi/
.agents/
.commands_synced
data/
logs/
hf-cache/
ollama-models/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.migrate-staging/
discord_ai_bot.egg-info/
tests/
remote-pi-relay/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.log
